top to bottom direction
title Supporting boundaries · Processing control / idempotency · 76282d3
class SubmissionGuard <<independent cancellation gate>> $PROC {
 asset_id: UUID
 owner_id: UUID
 job_id: UUID | None
 deleted_at: datetime | None
}
class RetryRequest <<idempotency ledger>> $INFRA {
 id: UUID
 job_id: UUID
 request_id: UUID
 attempt_id: UUID
}
class AttemptTask <<execution binding ledger>> $INFRA {
 attempt_id: UUID
 task_name: str
}
class JobMessaging <<state-version ledger>> $INFRA {
 job_id: UUID
 state_version: int
}
SubmissionGuard -[hidden]right- RetryRequest
RetryRequest -[hidden]right- AttemptTask
AttemptTask -[hidden]right- JobMessaging
note bottom of SubmissionGuard
  _guard(): create + lock; check owner.
  _cancel_locked(): no-Job tombstone persists.
  Later submit is a no-op, not resurrection.
  Gate is NOT a Job child.
end note
note bottom of AttemptTask
  messaging.claim(): atomic task binding.
  PK attempt_id; UNIQUE task_name.
  emit_state(): increment JobMessaging;
  commit state + result (+ queued work).
end note
legend bottom
  Per guard: 0..1 Job (nullable local FK); inverse is not UNIQUE in SQL.
  Per Job: 0..* RetryRequest (UNIQUE job_id, request_id); per retry: 1 Job + 1 Attempt (FKs).
  Per Attempt: 0..1 AttemptTask; per Job: 0..1 JobMessaging (1 after V1 acceptance); both local FKs.
  All Media identities are plain UUIDs. Selected fields; supporting records are outside Job membership.
endlegend

